      "description": "Job Description - Marketing Part-Time, Adjunct Instructor, Spring 2027 (26006211) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Marketing Part-Time, Adjunct Instructor, Spring 2027 (26006211) Job Description Marketing Part-Time, Adjunct Instructor, Spring 2027 Bradford M&E-Business Management - Pennsylvania-Bradford - ( 26006211 ) Marketing Part-Time, Adjunct Instructor, Spring 2027 The Division of Management and Education at the University of Pittsburgh at Bradford is currently seeking a Part-Time, Adjunct Instructor of Marketing to join our business faculty for the Spring 2027 Term. The ideal candidate will bring real-world business expertise into the classroom to teach undergraduate courses in Marketing. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a closely related field. A Master’s degree is preferred. Minimum of 3–5 years of professional experience in International Marketing, Brand Management, Consumer Behavior, or Global Business Strategy. Previous teaching experience at the college or university level is highly preferred. Must be able to teach in-person courses at the University of Pittsburgh’s Bradford Campus, two to three days per week, during the Fall & Spring semesters with the possibility of evening course times. Responsibilities : Deliver engaging classroom instruction in Marketing. Preferred courses include International Marketing, Consumer Behavior, Marketing Research, Marketing Management, Principles of Marketing, etc. Integrate current industry trends, case studies, and professional experience into the curriculum to prepare students for marketing careers. Design and grade assignments, projects, and examinations. Provide constructive feedback to support student success. Candidates experienced in working with college students from varied backgrounds and who have applied experience in the field of expertise are encouraged to apply. Apply online at: https://www.join.pitt.edu/ . Please submit a letter of application; C.V.; statement of teaching philosophy; and contact information for five professional references, including their name, title, email address, phone number, and their relation to the candidate. (Please Note: All documents must be submitted as PDF files & labeled accurately in Talent Center.) Review of complete applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. www.upb.pitt.edu/faculty-search-information *Please Note: This Job Classification Does Not Support Sponsorship or Relocation. Please submit a letter of application; C.V.; statement of teaching philosophy; and contact information for five professional references, including their name, title, email address, phone number, and their relation to the candidate. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Bradford Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Teaching Statement, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
